\newlabel{fig:alpha_sweep}{{8}{26}{$\alpha $-mixing sweep at 1024 calibration samples. ADC PPL is minimized at $\alpha = 0.5$; smaller values under-weight the ADC regime, larger values amplify gradient noise from the floor operator and degrade no-ADC PPL}{figure.caption.29}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Loss-landscape visualisation around the converged transforms for $\alpha \in \{0, 0.5, 1\}$ via filter-normalized random perturbations. The $\alpha = 0.5$ minimum is the widest and flattest, indicating that mixed FP/ADC calibration finds smoother solutions than either extreme.}}{26}{figure.caption.30}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:loss_landscape}{{9}{26}{Loss-landscape visualisation around the converged transforms for $\alpha \in \{0, 0.5, 1\}$ via filter-normalized random perturbations. The $\alpha = 0.5$ minimum is the widest and flattest, indicating that mixed FP/ADC calibration finds smoother solutions than either extreme}{figure.caption.30}{}}
